# Environment variables Pages still reads.
#
# Port, database path, and the setup state are not configured here: they live
# in ~/.pages/config.toml (see README), and start parameters such as --port
# override that file. The variables below are older switches.
#
# Pages does not load this file by itself. Export the variables in the shell
# or in the service definition, or start the server with
# `node --env-file=.env server.mjs`.

# Key that encrypts stored GitHub tokens: 64 hexadecimal characters
# (32 bytes). Without it, Pages creates a key file next to the database.
# Back the key up together with the database; tokens cannot be read without it.
# PAGES_GITHUB_TOKEN_KEY=

# Secure attribute of the session and language cookies: true or false.
# Default: set when the request came in over HTTPS (also as reported by a
# reverse proxy in X-Forwarded-Proto), not set over plain HTTP. Browsers drop
# Secure cookies on plain HTTP outside of localhost.
# PAGES_COOKIE_SECURE=

# Set to 1 to log server cache hits, misses and invalidations.
# PAGES_CACHE_DEBUG=

# Development only: log statements slower than this many milliseconds
# (default 50).
# PAGES_SLOW_QUERY_MS=

# Mode of the production server; server.mjs sets production when unset.
# NODE_ENV=production
